  "probe": "embodied_affect_interoception (board #49)",
  "verdict": "GO (6-seed) \u2014 a SIMULATED INTEROCEPTIVE BODY-STATE causally drives the NEURAL affect attractor, and interoception is LOAD-BEARING. Sweeping the body: a comfortable body -> POSITIVE felt valence (mood +0.082), a distressed body -> NEGATIVE valence (-0.081) (swing 0.163, ordered corr +0.84); an aroused body RAISES felt arousal (swing 0.082). Cutting the interoceptive->affect SYNAPSES DECOUPLES the feeling from the body (valence range 0.181 -> 0.000, corr +0.84 -> +0.00; arousal range 0.107 -> 0.000) while the interoceptive pools STILL encode the body (6/6 seeds, corr +0.99 intact). The affect read is the attractor's OWN rate(V+)-rate(V-); the body reaches it ONLY through synapses (asserted). CHARACTERIZED BOUNDARY (reported, not gated) \u2014 the affect reads the body as a BISTABLE SWITCH, not a graded circumplex: mood is a two-state signed latch (comfortable +0.082 / distressed -0.081, flipping sign near the set-point) and felt-arousal is an on/off ignition (arousal gradedness Pearson +0.70, 1/6 seeds >=0.8; a smooth ramp would read ~0.95). This is the SAME P0.3 bistable-latch limit \u2014 a graded valence x arousal continuum needs the named line/bump attractor + dendritic surpass. It does NOT weaken the embodiment claim: the body still CAUSES the correct signed feeling and interoception is load-bearing. numpy-CPU; NO sim/ edit (additive extra_regions/extra_pathways seam).",
